WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.862
Security teams rely heavily on alerts generated by SIEMs, EDR platforms, firewalls,

00:00:04.862 --> 00:00:06.449
and other security technologies.

00:00:06.449 --> 00:00:12.005
Those tools are important, but they do not reveal every important security event automatically.

00:00:12.005 --> 00:00:15.973
Some threats may use legitimate tools, valid credentials, novel techniques,

00:00:15.973 --> 00:00:19.544
or low-and-slow approaches designed to blend into normal activity.

00:00:19.544 --> 00:00:23.116
If defenders only investigate what already triggered an alert,

00:00:23.116 --> 00:00:25.100
hidden activity may remain unnoticed.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:31.449
Threat hunting exists because defenders cannot assume that everything important will appear in an alert queue.

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:36.211
Hunting is a proactive effort to search for suspicious activity that may

00:00:36.211 --> 00:00:38.592
have gone undetected by existing controls.

00:00:38.592 --> 00:00:42.560
A mature SOC uses alerts, investigations, incident response, detection engineering,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.544
threat intelligence, and hunting together.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:48.116
Hunting helps the team ask better questions, test assumptions,

00:00:48.116 --> 00:00:50.100
and improve visibility over time.
